  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Local Governance for Sustaining Peace in Two (2) PDET Subregions in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s objective is to promote peaceful and inclusive societies for sustainable development in two Development Plans with a Territorial Focus (PDET) subregions, which span three departments and 21 municipalities. The project&#x2019;s expected primary outcome is that within four years of implementation, communities from the two prioritized PDET regions have contributed to sustaining locally-led peace, by strengthening capacities to promote peacebuilding and self-management for violence prevention. This project seeks to continue strengthening Peace Agreement implementation, by promoting institutional, community, and relational capacity building among the different population groups and institutions in the prioritized territories; with the construction or refurbishing of physical spaces for coexistence and reconciliation, training for social leaders, the implementation of programs that provide services to population groups who merit a differential approach and have coexisted in contexts of violence and illegality. Thus, the project seeks to design and implement methodologies with a community, prevention, and human rights approach that will strengthen the civic role of the National Police.</narrative>
  </description>
